# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
#
# Without this the context is ~138 MB — node_modules, build output and your
# actual catalogue database all get shipped to the daemon on every build. The
# Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and `npm run build` itself, so none of it is wanted;
# copying host build output in would also mean the image could contain artifacts
# that were never built from the committed source.

# NOTE: .dockerignore does NOT match basenames at any depth the way .gitignore
# does — a bare `*.tsbuildinfo` matches only the context root. Every pattern
# below therefore needs its `**/` twin.
#
# Getting this wrong is not loud. A stale packages/*/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo copied
# from the host makes `tsc -b` believe the build is already up to date, so it
# emits nothing, and the image ends up missing dist entirely.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime data — never build a database or someone's library into an image
data
downloads
library
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.git
.github
.gitignore
.env
.env.local

# Tests and fixtures are not needed at runtime and are the bulk of the source
**/test
coverage

# Docs — not needed at runtime
*.md
docs

.DS_Store
*.log
